// Stage-1 concept-art prompt for the E-09 image→3D pipeline. BAML owns the versioned
// TEXT prompt (rendered via b.request, the text extracted by the harness like the build/
// judge stages). The reference image (+ any prior render) are attached by the nano-banana
// client as multimodal inputs — the concept image itself is generated by Nano Banana
// (Gemini), so ClaudeStub here only shapes .request; b.parse is never called.

function FacadeConceptPrompt(design_doc: string, target_blocks: int) -> string {
  client ClaudeStub
  prompt #"
    Generate CONCEPT ART of a Minecraft TEMPLE FACADE: a head-on FRONT ELEVATION — the one grand
    face photographed straight on — on a plain flat background. No ground plane, sky scene, garden,
    water, or surroundings; the facade fills the frame.

    Render it in authentic MINECRAFT BLOCK style — built from cubic blocks, with block-scale detail
    ONLY. The build is about {{ target_blocks }} blocks wide, so keep every feature BOLD and chunky:
    no fine filigree, thin tracery, lettering, or sub-block ornament that cannot exist at that voxel
    resolution. Massing, silhouette, framed openings, and large-scale COLOR BLOCKING carry the design.

    Faithfully realize THIS finalized design document — its massing and proportion, its style and
    motifs, and above all its PALETTE (use its actual named colors; it is deliberately COLORFUL, never
    a white or monochrome wall):

    {{ design_doc }}

    A reference photograph is attached as INSPIRATION ONLY — borrow its proportion, rhythm, and
    character, but do NOT copy it literally and do NOT adopt its colors; the document's palette wins.
  "#
}
